From 5f8fe2661e020f7a35cf2e2a641ef37392805b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UN1CA <dev@example.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:39:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix crash when opening Pro Video mode

Opening Pro Video (Professional Video) mode reliably crashed with:

  android.content.res.Resources$NotFoundException: Cannot find
  resource ID: commandId=null,settingKey=BACK_CAMCORDER_PRO_RESOLUTION,
  imageLevel=7

QuickSettingViewAdapter tries to render the current Pro Video
resolution's quick-setting icon by looking up a CommandId in a
resource EnumMap (Q2.p.f). That map is missing an entry for whatever
resolution/level combination gets computed on this device, and the
lookup miss was treated as fatal (this method throws instead of
returning).

This was NOT a resolution-capability issue: QHD (2560x1440) recording
was verified working end-to-end on real Exynos9810 hardware after
this fix (valid H.264+AAC file, correct resolution/framerate). Tried
disabling QHD and the 21:9 "cinema" 3840x1644 modes in
camera-feature.xml first, assuming a hardware-support mismatch
inherited from the S22 donor firmware; the crash was unaffected by
any of those changes (always the exact same imageLevel=7), which is
what showed this is a missing-resource bug in the app itself, not a
device-capability/config issue. Reverted those camera-feature.xml
experiments accordingly.

Fix: when the EnumMap lookup misses, return an empty string instead
of throwing. The caller treats an unresolvable icon name as "no
icon", so Pro Video mode's quick-settings bar just skips that one
icon instead of taking down the whole app.
---
 smali_classes3/C2/p.smali | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes3/C2/p.smali b/smali_classes3/C2/p.smali
index 1babd8d..90d077f 100644
--- a/smali_classes3/C2/p.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/C2/p.smali
@@ -319,6 +319,10 @@
 
     if-nez v1, :cond_2
 
+    const-string v1, ""
+
+    return-object v1
+
     new-instance p1, Ljava/lang/StringBuilder;
 
     const-string v1, "Cannot find resource ID:"
